  "correct": "4",
  "solution": "[IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/e306d0edaa1c360a9dc63af39b3f34da9440d14853e714d54d6553647fbc3ba8.png] \n\nGiven equation: 10 - 26 + 12 × 20 ÷ 5 = 18\n\nOption 1) 18 and 10\n\nAfter interchanging the numbers we get:\n\n⇒ 18 - 26 + **__12 × 20 ÷ 5__** = 10\n\n⇒ __**18**__ - 26 + __48__ = 10\n\n⇒ **__66 - 26__** = 10\n\n⇒ 40 = 10\n\nOption 2) 12 and 18\n\nAfter interchanging the numbers we get:\n\n⇒ 10 - 26 + __**18 × 20 ÷ 5**__ = 12\n\n⇒ __**10**__ - 26 + __72__ = 12\n\n⇒ __**8**____**2 - 26**__ = 12\n\n⇒ 56 = 12\n\nOption 3) 12 and 26\n\nAfter interchanging the numbers we get:\n\n⇒ 10 - 12 + __**26 × 20 ÷ 5**__ = 18\n\n⇒ __**10**__ - 12 + __104__ = 18\n\n⇒ __**114 - 12**__ = 18\n\n⇒ 102 = 18\n\n**Option 4) 10 and 20**\n\nAfter interchanging the numbers we get:\n\n⇒ 20 - 26 + __**12 × 10 ÷ 5**__ = 18\n\n⇒ 20 - 26 + __12 × 2__ = 18\n\n⇒ __**20**__ - 26 + __24__ = 18\n\n⇒ __44** - 26**__ = 18\n\n**⇒ 18 = 18**\n\nHence, the correct answer is **\"**10 and 20\".",
